          points: ['What the law or rule is', 'When and where it applies', 'Why it was introduced', 'And explain why you think it is a good law'],
          sample: 'A law that I strongly support is the rule that everyone travelling in a car must wear a seat belt, including passengers in the back seats. In my country this law applies at all times, whenever a car is moving, and the driver is responsible if the passengers break it.\n\nThe law was introduced because thousands of people were dying in road accidents that they could have survived. Before the law, many drivers thought seat belts were uncomfortable or unnecessary, especially on short journeys. In fact, most accidents happen close to home, on exactly those short journeys.\n\nI think this is an excellent law for several reasons. First of all, it clearly saves lives — hospitals reported a big fall in serious head injuries after it was introduced. Secondly, it costs the public nothing; you only have to spend two seconds putting the belt on. Finally, it creates a good habit, so children who grow up wearing seat belts continue the habit as drivers themselves.\n\nOf course, some people complain that the government should not control such personal choices. However, when an unbelted passenger is injured, it is the public health service and the family who pay the price. For me, this law is a perfect example of a simple rule that prevents a huge amount of suffering, and I believe every country should have it.'
