      writing: {
        task1: {
          title: 'Average household size, 1960–2020',
          text: 'The line graph below shows the average number of people per household in one country between 1960 and 2020.\n\nIn 1960 the average household contained 4.6 people. This fell steadily to 3.8 in 1980 and 3.1 in 2000, before levelling off at 2.9 in 2020.\n\nSummarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\nWrite at least 150 words.',
          sample: 'The line graph shows how the average size of a household in one country changed between 1960 and 2020.\n\nOverall, households became significantly smaller over the sixty-year period. The average number of people per household fell in every twenty-year interval, although the decrease became much slower after 2000.\n\nIn 1960, the average household contained 4.6 people, which suggests that large families and extended households were still common. Over the following twenty years, the figure declined steadily, reaching 3.8 people per household by 1980.\n\nThe fall continued between 1980 and 2000, and by the turn of the century the average household had shrunk to 3.1 people. This was the same rate of decline as in the previous period, a drop of 0.7 people in twenty years.\n\nAfter 2000, however, the trend almost stopped. By 2020 the average had fallen only slightly, to 2.9 people per household. In total, the average household in 2020 was barely more than half the size of its 1960 equivalent.\n\nIn summary, the country experienced a long and steady move towards smaller households, with the fastest changes taking place in the second half of the twentieth century.'
        },
        task2: {
          title: 'Children and grandparents',
          text: 'In many countries, grandparents play an important role in bringing up their grandchildren. Some people believe this is entirely positive, while others think children should be raised only by their parents.\n\nDiscuss both views and give your own opinion.\n\nGive reasons for your answer and include any relevant examples from your own knowledge or experience.\n\nWrite at least 250 words.',
          sample: 'In many cultures, grandparents are deeply involved in the daily care of their grandchildren. While some people welcome this, others argue that raising children is the parents\' responsibility alone. In my opinion, grandparents can be a great benefit, as long as the parents remain in charge.\n\nThere are several strong arguments in favour of grandparents helping with childcare. Firstly, they provide free, loving care from someone the child already knows and trusts, which is far better than a stranger in an expensive nursery. In my country, for example, many mothers return to work a few months after giving birth, and grandparents make this possible. Secondly, the relationship is valuable in itself. Children who spend time with grandparents learn family traditions, hear stories about the past and develop patience and respect for old people. Grandparents, in return, feel needed and are less lonely.\n\nHowever, there is another side to the argument. Grandparents and parents often disagree about discipline, food and screen time, and a child can become confused — or learn to play one side against the other. An indulgent grandmother who allows unlimited sweets may undermine the parents\' rules. There is also the question of fairness: elderly people have earned their rest, and full-time childcare can be exhausting and damaging to their health.\n\nIn my view, the answer is balance. Parents must make the important decisions and set the rules, but within those rules, grandparents\' help should be welcomed, not rejected. Families have supported each other in this way for thousands of years, and modern parents, facing high housing costs and long working hours, need that support more than ever.\n\nIn conclusion, grandparents bring love, experience and practical help to a family, and children benefit enormously from their presence, provided that the parents keep the leading role.'
        }
      },
